In article <1992Aug10.002634.18024@cis.ohio-state.edu> fabian@cis.ohio-state.edu (anjanette louise fabian) writes:

>	I _fnally had a successful character and I saved
>my game.  The character had undergone a sex change and had a different name,
>from fabian to Lyasta.  I tried nethack 
>again and it didn't restore my save file (I know it is in the savedir).
>How do I get it back? Or did I NOT save it and just think I did.

	If this is NetHack on a UNIX system, try the command:
		nethack -u Lyasta
	That invokes the game with the character's name as Lyasta;
otherwise, invoking the game without the -u option uses your login
name (which I assume is fabian).

